The seven new cases cover starred/unstarred renamed display names, warmed and
new receiving fetchers, a new type-specific subject, reuse of the old canonical
name by a different coded Setting, rejection of a mismatched explicit alias
code, qualified general fallback, empty current content, codename revocation,
and an explicit multiword code whose display key singularizes.

